<h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-primary mb-4">Common Causes of Swelling Inside the Mouth</h2>
</div>
<div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Gum Swelling / Gumboil</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Swelling of the gums near a tooth — a gumboil — caused by a dental abscess at the root tip. A pus-filled swelling appears on the gum and may discharge into the mouth. Requires root canal or extraction of the source tooth. <a href="painful-gum-swelling-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Painful gum swelling</a> and <a href="pus-in-gums-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">pus in gums</a> pages cover these in detail.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Palatal Swelling</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Swelling on the roof of the mouth — from a dental origin (tooth root infection on upper teeth), salivary gland obstruction (palatal mucocele), or an enlarging cyst or tumour. Upper tooth root infections on the palate require urgent attention as they can spread toward the eye.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Salivary Mucocele / Ranula</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A cystic swelling from a blocked or damaged minor salivary gland — appears as a bluish-clear swelling on the inner lip, floor of mouth, or palate. A ranula is a large mucocele under the tongue. Requires surgical excision of the affected gland.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Pericoronitis</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Swelling of the gum flap over a partially erupted tooth — most commonly a lower wisdom tooth. The gum flap traps food and bacteria causing acute pain, swelling, and difficulty opening the mouth. <a href="bacterial-mouth-infection-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Bacterial mouth infection</a> covers this cause.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Torusal Exostosis</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Bony growths on the inside of the jaw — typically on the palate (palatal torus) or inside the lower jaw (mandibular torus). These are benign bony outgrowths that may grow large enough to interfere with dentures or chewing. Surgical removal is straightforward if needed.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Abscess / Space Infection</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A pus-filled intraoral swelling from a dental infection. A submasseteric or pterygomandibular space infection can cause severe trismus and throat swelling visible inside the mouth. Requires urgent IV antibiotics and drainage. <a href="severe-tooth-infection-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Severe tooth infection</a> has full details.</p></div>
</div>
