<p class="text-on-surface-variant mb-6">The location of intraoral swelling narrows the diagnosis significantly. Upper gum swelling → likely dental origin from upper teeth. Lower gum swelling → dental or periodontal origin. Floor of mouth → salivary gland or infection. Palatal swelling → tooth root, gland, or cyst.</p>
